-- title:
--   The subring generated by rational endomorphisms is already the set of rational endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an $F$-algebra structure, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$ which is elliptic. Let $\alpha$ be an additive endomorphism of the group of affine points $(W_k)(k)$ of the base change of $W$ to $k$. The assertion is that $\alpha$ lies in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring k W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32), the subring of $\operatorname{End}((W_k)(k))$ generated by [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) (multiplication being composition of additive maps), if and only if the underlying additive map of $\alpha$ already lies in [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet k W W`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28), that is: either $\alpha = 0$, or $\alpha$ is rationally represented in the following sense — there exist four bivariate polynomials $n_X, d_X, n_Y, d_Y \in F[X][Y]$ and a finite set $B \subseteq k$ such that for all $x, y \in k$ with $(x,y)$ a nonsingular point of $W_k$ and $x \notin B$, the values of $d_X$ and $d_Y$ at $(x,y)$ (after base change of coefficients to $k$) are nonzero and $\alpha$ sends the affine point $(x,y)$ to the affine point with coordinates $n_X(x,y)/d_X(x,y)$ and $n_Y(x,y)/d_Y(x,y)$. Thus the generating set is closed under the subring operations.
--
--   In the points-level formulation of the endomorphism ring of an elliptic curve used here, this says that the subring generated by the $F$-rationally represented additive self-maps of $W(k)$ coincides with that set of maps; it corresponds to the classical fact that $\operatorname{End}_F(W)$ consists of morphisms of curves. It allows results proved for rationally represented maps — factorisation through $[n]$, duals, rigidity — to be applied to arbitrary elements of the endomorphism ring, and is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld material on kernel ideals and Frobenius conjugation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_mem_rationalEndSubring_iff_mem_rationalHomSet.lean

